     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>Note: In the context of cannabis, “primary” and “secondary” terpenes refer to their concentration and influence on a strain’s characteristics, specifically its taste, aroma, and effects. Primary terpenes are the most dominant and play a significant role in shaping a strain’s profile, while secondary terpenes contribute in smaller amounts, adding layers and nuances to the overall experience. <strong>*Terpene percentage values in each product should give you a better understanding of its profile.</strong></p>",
